from navigating obstacle courses  to playing team sports  and creating handicrafts  120 000 palestinian children are  experiencing a typical summer holiday  i love the slide the jumping castle and  trampoline if there wasn't this summer  camp i would have been at home for the  entire vacation  the camp has a variety of activities  and lots of fun games i wish it was the  entire summer holiday but even though  it's for one week i have a lot of fun  and i am happy  the initiative is organized by the un  relief and works agency for palestine  refugees  these summer camps last only for one  week but they provide a lot of support  physical and mental activities for the  children of gaza it's a small gesture  that makes a big difference in the lives  of these impoverished children  more than a million people defend a new  agency for food health care and  education assistance and families spend  the little money they do have on food  rather than entertainment  but these camps are about more than just  fun and games  the un says they provide indirect  psychological support to children  traumatized by the war  educational activities aimed at helping  the youngsters to manage loss anger and  stress  if you track the symptoms and signs of  children and as i will find higher rates  of trauma symptoms  higher rates of anxiety high rates of  you know sadness and so on  and one study that was published by save  the children foundation they recorded  almost 80 percent of such symptoms among  children  the camps may last only 7 days  but for these children it's a chance to  enjoy the simple pleasures other  youngsters take for granted  you must see it al jazeera gaza
 

